<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kissamos</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kastelli Kissamou, Kisamos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kissamos is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-kissamos">Gulf of Kissamos</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, also known as Kastelli. In antiquity Kisamos served as the harbour of the hill city of Polyrrhenia and later became a city in its own right, with a bishopric in Roman and Byzantine times. Excavations have uncovered Roman houses with fine mosaics, shown in the town's museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kissamos.jpg" alt="Kissamos" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin Belam from Chania, Crete · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2339_kissamos-kastelli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
